text:
The field is as white as snow;
As soft are its petals’ glow;
I pluck them for myself, but they will not stay on my hands!
Though this world may never be seen again,
What am I saying? The Earth is still here;
All that I need is right in front of me.

Kashf Al-Ghummah, by Shaikh Muhammad ibn Abdul Wahhab

I was lost in my own darkness;
Lost in my thoughts and unaware.
In deep contemplation I pondered;
On what is good or evil to me?

The world around me looked grey and black;
All seemed so distant from me!
But then, suddenly it dawned on me:
That God has blessed me with His mercy!

He drew on his long store of memories, that no wind could blow away:
the old sea-captain's stories of pirates and black-skinned men;
and tales from school books about King Arthur and Queen Guinevere.
